WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
SPEAKER: Today in
America, there really

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:05.430
is only one unforgivable
sin and that

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.370
is to deviate from
the accepted script

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:13.200
when speaking of
protected identity groups.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.130
It is to say something,
whether intentionally or not,

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.220
that either offends
protected identity groups

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.370
or that the elites find
offensive on their behalf.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.610
What I think is important
to grasp from the outset

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.790
is that identity
politics today is not

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.330
just the dominant ideology
when it comes to civil rights,

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:36.720
it's the dominant ideology
in America period.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.890
If you look at prominent
politicians, professors,

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:45.960
producers, pundits, fortune 500
CEOs, tech gurus, journalists,

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.840
all of the famous credentialed
and successful people

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:51.630
who comprise our ruling
class, they either

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.510
all affirm the tenets
of identity politics,

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.850
or at the very least
are deferential to them.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.890
Americans are now divided into
favored and disfavored groups,

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.200
and civil rights
law, we are told,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.230
should not apply to
the favored groups.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.560
Identity politics is demanding
that we judge people,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:12.960
not by the content
of their character,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.030
but by the color of
their skin, their sex,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.010
and their sexual orientation.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:20.580
And it demands that we
do so in perpetuity.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:23.970
It rejects the principle
of what James Madison once

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:27.180
called equal rights
under equal laws,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.020
and it instead demands that
we build a modern caste

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.880
system that privileges some
groups over others in our laws

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.900
and culture.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.660
Identity politics is not
answering the question,

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.610
who am I, although it does have
an answer to that question.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:48.720
Its primary focus, rather,
is the much deeper question

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:52.140
of why is there
evil in the world,

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:57.120
and identity politics provides
a clear and unambiguous answer

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:58.890
because of straight white men.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:03.630
Identity politics takes and
modifies the Christian teaching

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.300
on sin and now no longer
applies to everyone but only

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.560
to the oppressor groups.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.320
But here's the more
important modification.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.340
It offers no hope of salvation
or redemption from sin.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.440
Equal group outcomes are now the
measure of equal opportunities

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.060
between groups.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.150
And under this logic,
all disparities

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:27.990
can only have one
explanation, discrimination.

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.570
All disparities are
blamed on discrimination,

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:34.350
and anyone who suggests
otherwise is immediately

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:37.530
called a sexist and
a racist in order

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:41.040
to silence dissent
and stymie inquiry.

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:44.790
And here of course ultimately
is the great paradox

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:47.490
of this focus on group results.

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.670
It requires
discrimination, in order,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.130
it says, to eliminate
discrimination.

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:57.570
If you focus on results,
this will inevitably

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:02.340
lead you to deny positions
to some people on the basis

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:05.530
of their skin color, their race,
their ethnicity, their sex,

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.800
their sexual
orientation, you name it.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.230
The main reason that
identity politics

00:03:10.230 --> 00:03:14.070
exerts such a powerful
pull in America

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:17.700
is because it suggests that
we can either embrace identity

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.740
politics or remain callously
indifferent to the well-being

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:26.550
of fellow Americans who
happen not to look like us.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:29.970
This, in truth,
is a false choice.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:32.670
Identity politics
should be rejected,

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.130
not because it demands
justice for those

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:39.610
who have been unjustly treated,
but because it poses a threat

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:44.230
to Republican self-government
by corroding patriotic ties

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:46.690
and demanding special
treatment rather

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:48.130
than equality under the law.

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:51.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

